# ScaleSnap - Product Master List

ScaleSnap is a high-precision 3D visualization platform built to remove the "size guessing game" for online shopping.
It gives both consumers and businesses a way to compare real-world dimensions using familiar household anchors.

## 1) Product Environments

### A) Consumer Utility Portal
- **Who it serves:** Individual shoppers
- **Core action:** Enter custom dimensions and render a 3D box in a comparison stage
- **Anchors:** Everyday objects (for example: soda can, gallon jug, credit card, standard doorway)
- **Pricing:** $10.99/month
- **Trial:** First 3 renders free, paywall on 4th attempt

### B) Professional Business Suite
- **Who it serves:** E-commerce brands, sellers, and product teams
- **Core action:** Create permanent, locked "Visual Dimension Links" for products
- **Public experience:** Customers open a shareable URL and view a tamper-proof 3D comparison scene
- **Pricing:** $29.99/month
- **Value proposition:** Higher buyer confidence, fewer returns, stronger digital showroom experience

## 2) Core Website Modules (Cursor-Ready Master List)

### 2.1 Compare-to-Reality Engine
**Purpose**
- Render a precise 3D bounding box from user-entered dimensions
- Place the box next to selected anchors at true proportional scale

**Functional Requirements**
- Input fields for width, height, depth (with unit support and conversion)
- Real-time 3D updates without page reloads
- Anchor add/remove/swap controls
- Camera controls (orbit, zoom, pan)
- Optional "reset view" and "fit all objects" actions
- Visual labels for dimensions

**Implementation Notes**
- Frontend 3D layer (for example: Three.js or React Three Fiber)
- Shared scale normalization utility
- Validation pipeline for impossible/invalid dimensions

---

### 2.2 Secure-Link Vault
**Purpose**
- Store business product dimensions and generate immutable public links

**Functional Requirements**
- Authenticated business dashboard for creating product entries
- Server-side generation of unique URL tokens/IDs
- Non-editable public viewer route for each saved item
- Version-safe records (avoid accidental mutation of published links)
- Link metadata (created date, creator, product name, dimensions, anchor preset)

**Implementation Notes**
- Database tables for businesses, products, dimension snapshots, and public links
- Signed or random high-entropy IDs for link security
- Optional audit trail for updates/new versions

---

### 2.3 Anchor Gallery
**Purpose**
- Provide a curated library of real-world reference objects by size category

**Functional Requirements**
- Categories: Small, Medium, Large
- Search and quick-select UI in the 3D stage
- Standardized metadata per anchor:
  - Display name
  - Canonical dimensions
  - Unit standard
  - 3D asset path
  - Category tags
- Preset bundles (for example "kitchen set", "office set")

**Implementation Notes**
- Asset manifest JSON for anchor definitions
- CDN/static asset pipeline for optimized 3D models
- Consistent object origin and scale rules for all assets

---

### 2.4 Usage Monitor (Trial + Paywall Trigger)
**Purpose**
- Enforce "3 Free Tries" for guests and business prospects
- Trigger Stripe checkout on the 4th attempt

**Functional Requirements**
- Track render attempts by session/user/account
- Handle both anonymous and authenticated users
- Graceful upgrade prompts at trial boundary
- Stripe plan mapping:
  - Consumer plan: $10.99/month
  - Business plan: $29.99/month
- Webhook handling for subscription state sync

**Implementation Notes**
- Server-side counters to avoid client tampering
- Idempotent billing and webhook processing
- Trial status endpoint for UI gating logic

## 3) Suggested Data Model (MVP)

- `users` (id, role, email, auth_provider, created_at)
- `subscriptions` (user_id, tier, stripe_customer_id, stripe_subscription_id, status, renews_at)
- `usage_events` (id, user_id nullable, session_id, event_type, created_at)
- `anchors` (id, name, category, width, height, depth, unit, asset_url, is_active)
- `products` (id, business_user_id, name, sku, created_at)
- `dimension_snapshots` (id, product_id, width, height, depth, unit, locked_hash, created_at)
- `visual_links` (id, product_id, snapshot_id, public_token, is_active, created_at)

## 4) Suggested Route Map (MVP)

- `/` - marketing + product explainer
- `/consumer` - Consumer Utility Portal
- `/business` - Business Suite landing + onboarding
- `/dashboard/products` - business product management
- `/v/:publicToken` - locked public Visual Dimension Link page
- `/pricing` - tier comparison and CTA

### API Endpoints (example)
- `POST /api/render/attempt` - increment usage attempt
- `GET /api/trial/status` - remaining free tries
- `GET /api/anchors` - fetch anchor gallery metadata
- `POST /api/business/products` - create product
- `POST /api/business/products/:id/publish-link` - create immutable public link
- `POST /api/billing/create-checkout-session` - Stripe checkout
- `POST /api/billing/webhook` - Stripe webhook receiver

## 5) Acceptance Criteria Checklist

- [ ] 3D stage maintains accurate relative scale between custom box and anchors
- [ ] Anchor swaps are instant and maintain scene scale integrity
- [ ] 3 free render attempts are enforced for guests and prospects
- [ ] 4th attempt reliably routes to Stripe paywall
- [ ] Business users can create a locked Visual Dimension Link
- [ ] Public link view is read-only and cannot mutate stored dimensions
- [ ] Subscription status is synced from Stripe webhooks

## 6) Positioning Statement

ScaleSnap brings physical scale to digital commerce. By pairing high-precision 3D dimension rendering with familiar anchors and secure share links, it turns abstract measurements into immediate visual trust.
